30	 * statuses one at a time. Only a DRAFT can be edited. A voided claim keeps
31	 * its number, which is never reused; a claim opened while period numbering is on is numbered within its
32	 * period instead of sheet-wide. Settling a claim fixes its due at the rate its person's grade has then on the claim's date
33	 * (at least the sheet's floor then), or at the
34	 * figure a statement bound it to, plus the late charge it has then. No claim dated inside a closed period can be added, edited or moved,
35	 * and no claim dated after its person's retirement date can be added or edited to that date. A clerk
36	 * settling a claim whose due is above the sheet's clerk limit leaves it PENDING instead; a steward settles
37	 * anything, and approves a PENDING claim (settling it, its due fixed then) or rejects it with a reason
38	 * (back to OPEN); the user who opened a claim cannot approve it. A steward re-settles a SETTLED claim,
39	 * fixing its due again at the figure it would have today as an OPEN claim bound by no statement. A claim
40	 * with a negative amount is a correction: it is added or edited only when it names, by number, a SETTLED
41	 * claim of the same person, and only a correction names one. A claim whose due is above the sheet's proof
42	 * threshold in force on its date cannot be settled or approved while it has no proof.
43	 */
44	@Service
45	public class ClaimService {
46	
47	    private final ClaimRepository claims;
48	    private final PersonRepository people;
49	    private final SheetService sheets;
50	    private final SheetRepository sheetRows;
51	    private final RateService rates;
52	    private final Rollup rollup;
53	    private final PeriodService periods;
54	    private final AccessService access;
55	    private final WatchService watches;
56	    private final ApplicationEventPublisher events;
57	
58	    public ClaimService(ClaimRepository claims, PersonRepository people, SheetService sheets,
59	            SheetRepository sheetRows, RateService rates, Rollup rollup, PeriodService periods, AccessService access,
60	            WatchService watches, ApplicationEventPublisher events) {
61	        this.access = access;
62	        this.watches = watches;
63	        this.rollup = rollup;
64	        this.periods = periods;
65	        this.claims = claims;
66	        this.people = people;
67	        this.sheets = sheets;
68	        this.sheetRows = sheetRows;
69	        this.rates = rates;
70	        this.events = events;
71	    }
